---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy policy" description="What data this website collects, why, how long it is kept and how to exercise your rights. No advertising cookies and no third-party ad tracking.">
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "Privacy" }]} />
  <section class="tight">
    <div class="wrap narrow prose">
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="small">Last updated: November 2026</p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        {site.brand} is a trading name of {site.company.legalNameEn}, registered in {site.company.city},
        {site.company.region}, {site.company.country} (USCC {site.company.uscc}). For any privacy question,
        including a request about your data, contact <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
        We are the controller for the business contact and order data described on this page.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>This website is static. It does not have accounts, a cart or a login, and it does not load advertising or analytics trackers. We collect only what is needed to answer an enquiry, prepare a quotation or fulfil an order; we do not ask for a date of birth, a government ID or payment-card details through the site.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Information you send us</strong> — name, company, email, phone or WhatsApp number, shipping address, and the artwork or specifications you attach.</li>
        <li><strong>Order information</strong> — what you ordered, quantities, prices and delivery details, kept for accounting and warranty purposes.</li>
        <li><strong>Server logs</strong> — the hosting provider records requests (IP address, user agent, timestamp) for security and abuse prevention.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Why we use it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To answer enquiries and prepare quotations.</li>
        <li>To produce and deliver an order, and to handle defects or returns.</li>
        <li>To meet accounting and tax obligations.</li>
        <li>To protect the site against abuse.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Legal bases (GDPR)</h2>
      <p>Where the GDPR applies: performance of a contract or steps before a contract (Article 6(1)(b)), legal obligation for tax records (6(1)(c)), and legitimate interests for security and fraud prevention (6(1)(f)).</p>

      <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>Only what is necessary: the printing and finishing partners producing your order, the carrier delivering it, and our email and hosting providers. We do not sell personal data.</p>

      <h2>International transfers</h2>
      <p>Production is in China and our team is based there, so enquiries and order data are processed in China. Where the GDPR applies, transfers rely on appropriate safeguards such as standard contractual clauses with our service providers.</p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>Enquiries that do not become orders: up to 24 months. Order and invoice records: as long as accounting law requires. Artwork files: deleted on request once production is complete, unless you ask us to keep them for reorders.</p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>You can ask for access, correction, deletion, restriction, portability, or object to processing. Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> and we will respond within 30 days. You can also complain to your local data protection authority.</p>
      <p>
        Where UK GDPR applies, the same rights apply and you may complain to the UK Information Commissioner’s
        Office. Where California law applies, you may request to know, delete or correct personal information, and
        to opt out of its sale or sharing. We do not sell personal information and we do not share it for
        cross-context behavioural advertising; the only sharing is with the production, carrier and email providers
        described above, for the purposes described above.
      </p>

      <h2>Security and retention</h2>
      <p>
        Access to enquiry and order data is limited to the people who need it to quote, produce or ship an order.
        We use access-controlled email and hosting accounts, and we do not ask for card details through this website.
        No system is perfectly secure; if a breach affects your rights, we will notify you and the relevant
        authority where the law requires it.
      </p>
      <p>
        We keep enquiry data for up to 24 months, order and invoice records for the period required by accounting
        law, and artwork for the production period unless you ask us to keep it for reorders. When data is no longer
        needed, we delete it or anonymise it.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>This site sets no advertising or analytics cookies. If that changes, this page will list them and ask for consent first. The host may set a short-lived security cookie; see the <a href="/cookies/">cookie page</a> for the current list.</p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>The site is a business service and is not directed at children under 16.</p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If the way we handle data changes — for example, if analytics or a quote form is added — this page will be
        updated before the change goes live, and the “last updated” date will change. The current version does not
        load advertising, analytics or embedded media.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
